# Command Query Responsibility Segregation (CQRS) Pattern — Production-Grade LLD Blueprint

---

## 1. REQUIREMENTS & SCOPE

### Core Functional Requirements

| # | Requirement | Description |
|---|-------------|-------------|
| FR-1 | **Command-side mutation** | The system must accept commands (`OpenAccount`, `DepositMoney`, `WithdrawMoney`, `CloseAccount`) that mutate the write model (aggregate) and emit domain events. Each command enforces business invariants (no negative balances, positive amounts, no operations on closed accounts). |
| FR-2 | **Query-side reads** | The system must support queries (`FindAccountById`, `ListAllAccounts`, `CountAccounts`, `FindAccountsByOwner`) that read from a denormalized, query-optimized read model — completely decoupled from the write model. |
| FR-3 | **Event-sourced write model** | The write side must persist domain events (not final state) in an `EventStore`. Aggregates are rebuilt by replaying their event stream, enabling full audit history and read-model rebuilds. |
| FR-4 | **Read model synchronization** | A projection (`AccountProjection`) must subscribe to domain events via an `EventBus` and update the read model (`AccountReadModel`) so queries reflect the latest command-side state. |
| FR-5 | **Account lifecycle** | The system must support the full account lifecycle: open → deposit/withdraw → close. Closed accounts are excluded from list and count queries but remain in the event store for audit. |

### Non-Functional Requirements

| # | Requirement | Description |
|----|-------------|-------------|
| NFR-1 | **Thread-safety** | All infrastructure components (`EventStore`, `AccountReadModel`, `EventBus`, `CommandBus`, `QueryBus`) must be thread-safe using `ConcurrentHashMap` and `CopyOnWriteArrayList` to support concurrent command dispatch and query execution without external locking. |
| NFR-2 | **Extensibility** | New commands, queries, events, and projections can be added without modifying existing handlers or buses — following the Open/Closed Principle. The `CommandHandler` and `QueryHandler` interfaces allow plug-and-play registration. |
| NFR-3 | **Immutability** | All model objects (commands, queries, events, `AccountView`) are immutable Java records — no shared mutable state between the write and read sides. The aggregate is the only mutable object, and it is not shared across threads. |

