### 3.2 Sequence Diagram — Deposit Money Command (Primary Use Case)

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Client as Client
    participant CmdBus as CommandBus
    participant Handler as DepositMoneyHandler
    participant Repo as AccountRepository
    participant Store as EventStore
    participant Agg as AccountAggregate
    participant Bus as EventBus
    participant Proj as AccountProjection
    participant ReadModel as AccountReadModel

    Client->>CmdBus: dispatch(DepositMoney(accountId, 200))
    CmdBus->>CmdBus: lookup handler for DepositMoney
    CmdBus->>Handler: handle(DepositMoney)

    Handler->>Repo: find(accountId)
    Repo->>Store: load(accountId)
    Store-->>Repo: [AccountOpened, ...]
    Repo->>Agg: new AccountAggregate(id)
    Repo->>Agg: replay(AccountOpened)
    Repo->>Agg: replay(MoneyDeposited)
    Repo-->>Handler: AccountAggregate (balance=100)

    Handler->>Agg: deposit(200)
    Agg->>Agg: apply(MoneyDeposited(id, 200))
    Agg->>Agg: balance = 300
    Agg-->>Handler: void

    Handler->>Repo: persist(account)
    Repo->>Agg: pullUncommittedEvents()
    Agg-->>Repo: [MoneyDeposited(id, 200)]
    Repo->>Store: save(id, [MoneyDeposited])
    Repo->>Bus: publish(MoneyDeposited)

    Bus->>Proj: onMoneyDeposited(MoneyDeposited)
    Proj->>ReadModel: findById(id)
    ReadModel-->>Proj: AccountView(balance=100)
    Proj->>ReadModel: upsert(AccountView(balance=300))

    Repo-->>Handler: void
    Handler-->>CmdBus: null
    CmdBus-->>Client: null

    Note over Client,ReadModel: Read model is now synchronized with write model
```

