| Component | Storage | Thread-Safety |
|-----------|---------|---------------|
| `EventBus` | `ConcurrentHashMap` + `CopyOnWriteArrayList` | Thread-safe pub/sub |

### 4.3 SOLID Principles Applied

| Principle | Application |
|-----------|-------------|
| **S**ingle Responsibility | Each handler processes one command/query type; the aggregate enforces only business rules; the repository only loads/saves; the projection only updates the read model |
| **O**pen/Closed | New commands, queries, events, and projections can be added by implementing the `Command`, `Query`, `DomainEvent`, `CommandHandler`, or `QueryHandler` interfaces — no existing code changes needed |
| **L**iskov Substitution | Any `CommandHandler` or `QueryHandler` implementation can substitute for its interface in the `CommandBus` or `QueryBus` |
| **I**nterface Segregation | `Command` and `Query` are separate marker interfaces; `CommandHandler` and `QueryHandler` are separate contracts — clients depend only on what they need |
| **D**ependency Inversion | Handlers depend on the `AccountRepository` and `AccountReadModel` abstractions (simplified for this example; in production, these would be interfaces) |

### 4.4 Thread-Safety Implementation

```java
// Event Store: ConcurrentHashMap for event streams
static final class EventStore {
    private final Map<String, List<DomainEvent>> streams = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
    // computeIfAbsent() + CopyOnWriteArrayList.addAll() are thread-safe
}

// Event Bus: ConcurrentHashMap + CopyOnWriteArrayList for pub/sub
static final class EventBus {
    private final Map<Class<?>, List<Consumer<?>>> subscribers = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
    // computeIfAbsent() + CopyOnWriteArrayList.add() are thread-safe
}

// Read Model: ConcurrentHashMap for views
static final class AccountReadModel {
    private final Map<String, AccountView> views = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
    // put(), get(), stream() are all thread-safe
}

// Command/Query Buses: ConcurrentHashMap for handler routing
static final class CommandBus {
    private final Map<Class<?>, CommandHandler<?, ?>> handlers = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
    // put(), get() are atomic
}

// Models: immutable records (no mutable state)
record AccountView(String id, String owner, int balance, boolean closed) {}
record AccountOpened(String aggregateId, String owner, int initialBalance) implements DomainEvent {}
```

